WEBVTT

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:06.040
I first met Shuu on the first day of kindergarten.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.380
Shuri made us cry a lot when we were kids.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.040
Shuri's <i>denki anma</i> really hurt.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.690
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 69 0 69

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.690
Grab ankles + foot stomps to groin. BAD!

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.190
Grab ankles + foot stomps to groin. BAD!

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.190
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 69 0 69

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:19.850
But back then, would've never imagined that this would happen even in my wildest dreams.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.150
I'll never forget Shuu.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.160
And of course, Shuri too.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.960
I'll never ever forget them.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.000
Morning Sana...

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.040
Nanaka?

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:57.880
Morning.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:06.620
Regardless of the subject,
 they're all basically written in Japanese.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:07.250
<b>Red Memories</b>

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:12.060
Searching for the correct
 answers is the fast track in life.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.280
However, obviously...

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:37.990
Did you hear about the twins from 2-F disappearing?

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.190
Yeah, I did. They were caught entering a love hotel...

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.620
...and their parents found out, right?

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.860
Wait, you mean incest?

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:50.650
Yeah, that's why they disappeared.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.670
Seriously?

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.170
Did you make all this, Aoi-chan?

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:04.920
I made lots, so have some too, Nanaka-chan.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:10.830
Sorry... I don't feel hungry.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.980
Neither do I...

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:19.830
I knew that you guys would be feeling down with Shuri-chan and Shuu-chan gone. {S: "Know" to "Knew"}

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.670
So, I made this to cheer you guys up.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.500
I'm sorry.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.560
Sorry.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.800
But, I really can't.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:36.570
I'm home.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.520
What's with Shuu?

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.560
He didn't have to keep it from me.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.430
Hidaka-san. A delivery for you.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.770
May I have your stamp please?

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.700
If you don't have one, then your signature will do. Here.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.750
<b>From:</b>

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.750
Wakatsuki Shuusuke

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.300
<b>Address</b>

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.300
<b>Phone Number</b>

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.300
<b>Special Promotion Now!!</b>

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.060
Would you like me to warm up the bento?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.660
Yes, please.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:37.570
We're having a special promotion right now, so please draw a ticket.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.310
You've won a drink.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:49.280
Thank you very much.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.520
Sensei.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.850
Hidaka-kun!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.450
May I join you?

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.450
Sure.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.400
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.820
You look down.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.700
I'm a bit depressed.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.580
It's regarding Wakatsuki-san and Wakatsuki-kun.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:34.090
I wanted to get to know my students better.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.830
But, now this happens.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:40.720
When they are having problems, wouldn't they want to seek advice from me?

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.560
I guess I must have been dreaming.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.790
Sensei.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:49.910
But, even if I were to actually give them advice...

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:53.110
...I'm sure there was nothing I'd be able to do for them.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:58.500
They probably never told me because they already knew that.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:02.940
But at the very least, I wanted to give them encouragement.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:07.560
Listening to them, and telling them to be strong and not give up.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.300
But, even that...

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.060
Sorry. I guess I do this to make me feel good about myself.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:17.400
Just like how I randomly give out caramels.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.900
That's not true!

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.830
That's definitely not true!

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:26.910
That's right. I got this from the convenience store earlier.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.490
Here you go.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.300
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 69 0 69

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.510
Regista is the company producing Myself; Yourself.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:30.890
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 69 0 69

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:34.770
It may not be caramel, but this is the reward for your effort.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.930
Well, it may be a bit brazen since I'm your student.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.870
A reward for me?

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.380
Do you feel any better?

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.430
Huh? Kotsuchi River?

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:21.000
Yeah, this Sunday. Let's enjoy ourselves there like last time.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.740
You'll be coming too, right, Aoi-chan?

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:26.400
Of course! I'll cook up a storm.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.810
Hello? This is Hidaka.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:44.680
Aoi-chan?

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:49.300
What's up? I was just about ready to go fetch you.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:51.860
What? A cold?

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:58.590
Sorry, I suddenly came down with something last night.

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:02.840
No, it's okay. You don't have to come visit.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:06.180
I'm sure I'll get well by tomorrow.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:09.740
Please go with Nanaka-chan today.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:13.130
Okay, so see you then.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.900
Mum! What are you doing?!

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:22.640
You sure sound healthy for someone with a cold. {S: Currected "You're" to "You"}

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:28.450
You're supposed to be going out with Sana-chan and Nanaka-chan today, aren't you?

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:30.640
Why did you lie to him?

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:34.850
I did tell Sana-chan that I'd go.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:38.600
I knew that he wanted to cheer Nanaka-chan and me up.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:43.220
Though I was really shocked when Shuri-chan and Shuu-chan left...

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:46.740
...I feel that the one most heavily affected was Nanaka-chan.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:51.490
Just when we thought that everything was great because Sana-chan came back, now they're gone.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:59.180
So, I figured that it'd be better if Sana-chan and Nanaka-chan went by themselves.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:07.360
Because, Nanaka-chan is the one who needs Sana-chan the most right now.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:11.110
But, you must be feeling quite down about it too, right?

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:13.260
I am.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:19.270
But, since I'm the eldest, I figured that I'd have to be strong.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.220
I see.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:25.200
I thought you were still a child, except for your boobs.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.670
But, I guess you really have grown up.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:30.040
Mum!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.800
It wasn't long ago when we still took baths together.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.540
There's nothing to be embarrassed about, right?

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:44.680
Wasn't long ago? We stopped taking baths together around when I was in middle school.

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:52.220
Then, to celebrate my daughter's coming of age, I'm going to bake a nice chocolate cake.

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:57.340
You're going to help out, right?

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:05.030
So, Aoi-chan won't be coming after all.

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:06.950
Hmm? What do you mean by 'after all'?

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:10.470
I got a call from her last night.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:14.310
She said that she might not be able to come today because she wasn't feeling well.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:16.550
So, that's how it went?

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.830
Is that what I think it is?

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.830
Yeah, it's the one Shuu bought from the money he saved from work.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.450
The courier company delivered it to my place the other day.

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:31.460
So that means...

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:37.080
Shuu was the sender, but he didn't write down his address.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:42.340
But, he enclosed a note which read, "This is a good rod, so please make good use of it."

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:45.950
I see...

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:58.390
Let's see. Like this here, then like this. Next is...

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.680
Are you all right?

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:03.930
It's all right. Just leave it to me.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.130
Got it!

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.390
Okay! I'm going to catch lots!

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:23.410
You took forever to prepare the lure.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.560
Are you really going to be able to catch any fish?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:28.940
You saw the one I caught last time, right?

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:32.370
But, you only managed to catch one.

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:35.160
Well, what can I say?

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:39.180
You know how the saying goes, "Watch a man closely, because after three days..."

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.550
How did it go again?

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:42.750
"...he'll improve tremendously."

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.400
Yeah, yeah. That's it!

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:55.100
What a waste renting all these.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:56.790
I'm such a disgrace.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:11:00.630
But, what should we do?
 I was planning to cook the fish I caught.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.920
I only brought riceballs for lunch.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.720
Not a problem. I've got you covered too.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.280
I brought some food to go with the rice.

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:12.570
Eh? But why?

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:17.460
I told you that Aoi-chan called me last night, right?

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:23.950
Aoi-chan said that I should cook for two, just in case.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.660
No one trusts me...

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:33.740
Well, that's the fruits of your labour. 
I don't think you have a right to complain.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.840
Exactly as you've said...

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.870
Hey, wait a minute.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:44.260
So, that means you cooked for me too?

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:47.690
Of course. What else could I have possibly meant?

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.930
I see. Right.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.620
What is it? Got a problem?

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:55.000
Of course not.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.980
Here, eat up.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.820
Uh... What's this?

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.640
Fried eggs and cookies.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:06.890
Quite a bold combination, if I do say so myself.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:11.920
Well, I can't help it since that's all I know how to make.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.970
Then, allow me to have some.

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:24.430
How is it?

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:27.100
It's good.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:29.340
Really? It's good?

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:32.500
I thought that it might be a bit burnt. Or I may have put too much salt. {S: Removed the first "it" "I thought it that it"}

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:37.440
There might be egg shells mixed inside, but is it still good in spite of that?

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:38.490
Yep.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:42.060
Because, you made it.

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:48.200
Stupid.

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:10.680
Say, Nanaka, once we're done cleaning up, would you like to walk up river?

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.060
There's something I'd like to show you.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.170
Sure, but what is it you wanna show me?

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:18.530
It's a surprise.

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:33.730
Hey, I don't think it's such a good idea to go so deep into the mountains.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:35.610
What if we get lost?

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:40.970
Don't worry, I remember all the possible landmarks. We'll be fine.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:47.720
You said the same thing for the fishing. Look how that turned out.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:50.770
We'll really be fine this time.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.820
Oh no! Rain!

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:59.800
Sana, it's raining.

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:02.080
Shouldn't we head back?

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:05.150
It's not much farther. Let's keep going.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.890
There's shelter up ahead.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:25.500
Nanaka, pass me the fishing rod.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.010
Of course.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:29.480
Nanaka, grab on.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.530
I'm glad we didn't get drenched.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:47.260
Sana, where are we?

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:48.910
It's a bear's den.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:51.290
There's a big one hibernating inside.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:55.590
I'm kidding.

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:59.020
Besides, bears don't hibernate at this time of the year.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:02.260
Sheesh, don't scare me like that.

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.210
Where are you going?

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:10.640
I said that there was something I wanted to show you, right?

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:20.510
It's not those hairy things that swarm at your feet and suck your blood, right?

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:26.360
I'm not sure what you presume it is, but it's definitely not that.

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:30.290
A dead end?

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.700
So, what is it you wanted to show me?

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:35.420
This is it.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:45.660
What do you think? It's beautiful, isn't it?

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.260
Amazing. It's just like the starry sky.

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:55.030
This is Shuu's and my secret place.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:16:02.170
We stumbled upon here when we travelled through the mountains to find the source of the river. {S: Travelled" to "traveled"}

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:09.390
Being such an incredible discovery, we promised each other that we'd never tell anyone about this place.

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:13.690
But, you broke that promise by telling me.

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:17.400
Yeah. Shuu might get angry if he found out.

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:20.550
I'll apologise the next time I see him.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.430
The next time you see him?

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.660
Hey, cut it out, Sana!

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:36.190
I'm not playing. The battery in the flashlight ran out, I think.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:39.390
Oh well.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:42.780
Let's take shelter here until the rain lets up.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.190
But...

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.570
Are you afraid of the dark?

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:48.170
Don't be silly.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.690
Of course I'm not.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:52.150
So, you're all right with it then?

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.520
Hey, Sana.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:03.350
What is it?

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:05.340
Can I ask you something?

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:07.970
Sure. What is it though?

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.090
That wrist watch of yours...

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:19.540
Was it a gift from your girlfriend or something?

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:27.450
Well, Shuu mentioned it when we all went to the spa that time.

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:32.570
So, is it really from...?

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:37.510
No, this isn't anything like that...

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:45.840
Can I ask you something now then?

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:53.020
Why did you put all those letters for me into the secret mailbox?

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:55.480
If you were suffering that much...

00:17:55.480 --> 00:18:00.880
If you really wanted my help, you should have mailed them directly to me.

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:02.980
Then, I'd definitely...

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:04.350
I was scared.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:10.710
After the fire, I realised how much I had changed.

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:13.090
I realised that I became a gloomy person.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:16.570
And I stopped playing the violin which I loved so much.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:19.770
So, you stopped playing the violin?

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:25.940
I don't know why. Even though I risked my life to save it from the fire...

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:30.010
But, why is it when I hold the violin in my hands I feel such pain inside?

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:31.710
My head would start to spin.

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:36.930
The doctor said that it may be related to my lost memories.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.880
I see.

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:42.170
Because I had changed so much...

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:47.300
...I thought that you might have changed as well while we were apart.

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:52.780
I became frightened by the fact that you might no longer be the Sana I once knew.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:56.940
So, I felt if I put the letters into the secret mail box...

00:18:56.940 --> 00:19:02.450
...that I would be able to reach the Sana I knew from elementary school.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:04.450
Nanaka...

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:09.020
But, you haven't changed at all.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:12.400
At the start, I thought that you may have changed a little.

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:14.870
But, you're definitely the Sana I knew from before.

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:20.680
The Sana I know. The Sana I love.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.440
Oh no. Did I fall asleep?

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:42.170
Sana, where did you go?

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:44.590
Answer me, Sana!

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:47.290
Sana?

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.330
Ah, you're up.

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:12.730
I didn't wake you because you were sleeping so peacefully.

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:16.650
Nanaka?

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:24.150
Watch out!

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:48.230
Nanaka, are you all right?

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:53.420
Nanaka, what's wrong?

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:57.300
I... remember...

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:01.100
...the fire... everything.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:03.430
I remember everything.

00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:08.460
Mum! Sensei! Dad!

00:21:09.190 --> 00:21:11.800
Nanaka! Snap out of it!

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:13.080
Nanaka!

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:15.640
I... I...

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:47.140
Next time on Myself; Yourself: Shackles.

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:52.770
If I had known... If I had known about these terrifying memories....

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:55.040
Shackles

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.050
I would have rather gone on never remembering.
